  "articleBody": "Choosing between a prefabricated shower pan and a custom mud-bed tile base is one of the most critical decisions when planning a bathroom remodel. Both options have distinct practical tradeoffs regarding budget, installation timeline, and long-term design flexibility.\n\nHow to Compare Your Options:\n- Prefabricated pans: Made of acrylic or composite materials, these provide a factory-tested waterproof base with built-in slope. They install in roughly one day, reduce labor costs, and offer easy maintenance, though they limit you to standard shapes and central or offset drain locations.\n- Custom tile bases: Built on a hand-floated mortar bed with a topical waterproofing membrane, tiled bases allow curbless accessibility, benches, and custom footprints. However, they require extended curing times for mortar, thinset, and grout, typically taking several working days to finish properly.\n- Maintenance tradeoffs: Pre-formed pans have no grout lines along the floor, minimizing scrubbing, while tile offers superior slip resistance and timeless visual appeal.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps:\nIf your project involves changing drain locations, building a barrier-free shower, or reinforcing subfloors for heavy stone, professional craftsmanship ensures a leak-free build. Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC delivers expert tile and bathroom renovations. Call 303-505-0866 to plan your upgrade.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
